---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const buildDate = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
const posts = (await getCollection("blog"))
  .sort((a, b) => +b.data.date - +a.data.date)
  .slice(0, 3);
---

<Base
  title="Mateo Cerri — tinkerer"
  description="I take things apart to see what else they could become. Agent tooling, computer vision, and low-level experiments from Rafaela, Argentina."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="site-head">
      <a class="site-name" href="/">Mateo Cerri</a>
      <nav class="site-nav">
        <a href="#now">Now</a>
        <a href="#work">Work</a>
        <a href="#experiments">Experiments</a>
        <a href="/blog">Blog</a>
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <h1>Mateo Cerri</h1>
      <p class="role">tinkerer.</p>
      <p>
        I take things apart to see what else they could become. I touch a bit
        of everything, from build caches in Rust to vision models to file
        formats I had no business decoding by hand, and I prefer showing
        commits over collecting labels.
      </p>
      <p>
        Advanced Computer Engineering student at UNRaf, working from Rafaela,
        Argentina. I take on selected freelance work. Remote,
        async-friendly; details on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="now">Now</h2>
      <p class="sec-note">what occupies the bench</p>
      <p>
        Most days go to my final project: automatic visual inspection for
        metal parts, training on a public benchmark and validating against
        real rejected pieces, running on CPU with a local panel. In the
        margins, a private Rust project around AI-assisted game creation
        (more when it is public) and the small utilities below.
      </p>

      <h2 id="work">Work</h2>
      <p class="sec-note">things built, each with its receipts</p>
      <ul class="index">
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">oct 2026</span>
            <span class="row-title">Tools that show their work</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            Coding agents that edit through opaque shell writes are
            unauditable, so I gave mine visible tools:
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/opencode-patchflow">anchor-based atomic edits</a>
            and
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/opencode-scriptbox">a registry of reusable scripts</a>.
            One call renamed a type across 70 files. Same family:
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/opencode-slim-output">a trace pruner</a>
            and
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/opencode-wsl-shim">a WSL toolchain shim</a>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">sep 2026</span>
            <span class="row-title">A daemon that records streams once</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/hlsd">hlsd</a> records HLS
            sources so that every segment is fetched exactly once and shared
            between overlapping recordings, assembling MP4 on demand. It
            complements yt-dlp where no extractor exists.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2026 – now</span>
            <span class="row-title">A wholesale store I still run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            A custom e-commerce platform for a wholesaler,
            <a href="https://beccariamayorista.com.ar/">Beccaria Mayorista</a>:
            storefront, admin tools, order flows. I designed and deployed it,
            and I still maintain it
            <span class="meta">(Astro, React, AdonisJS, PostgreSQL)</span>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">dec 2023</span>
            <span class="row-title">A signal bench for a microcontroller</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/SerialPlotter">SerialPlotter</a>
            trades samples with a microcontroller over a serial port, plots
            them live, runs an FFT to show the harmonics, filters the signal
            and sends it back.
            <span class="meta">(C, FFTW, ImPlot)</span>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">jan 2023</span>
            <span class="row-title">An interpreter for an esoteric language</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            A <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri/Golfscript">GolfScript interpreter</a>
            in C#, written as a challenge with folks from Stack Overflow,
            back when AI assistance was more trouble than help. Unit tests
            included.
            <span class="meta">(C#, .NET)</span>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="writing">Recent writing</h2>
      <p class="sec-note">from the blog</p>
      <ul class="index">
        {
          posts.map((post) => (
            <li>
              <div class="row-head">
                <span class="row-date">
                  {post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}
                </span>
                <span class="row-title">
                  <a href={`/blog/${post.id.replace(/\.mdx?$/, "")}`}>{post.data.title}</a>
                </span>
              </div>
              <p class="row-desc">{post.data.description}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2 id="experiments">Experiments</h2>
      <p class="sec-note">an ongoing habit</p>
      <p>
        I like finding out how things work: sitting with a spec until bytes
        become pixels, wiring a sensor just to watch it report back. Most of
        these never shipped and several stalled halfway, done the hard way
        with barely any autocomplete. The understanding was the point, not
        the release. The habit stuck.
      </p>

      <h2 id="record">Record</h2>
      <p class="sec-note">for the scanners</p>
      <ul class="index">
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2021 – now</span>
            <span class="row-title">Computer Engineering, UNRaf</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            B.S. in progress. Final project: automatic visual inspection
            for metal parts.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2026 – now</span>
            <span class="row-title">Independent developer</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            Custom e-commerce platform for a wholesaler: designed, deployed,
            maintained.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2024 – 2025</span>
            <span class="row-title">Huawei ICT Competition, second prize</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">Cloud track.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2024 – 2025</span>
            <span class="row-title">AWS Academy graduate ×3</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            Cloud Architecting, Machine Learning for NLP, Cloud Foundations.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="row-head">
            <span class="row-date">2020 – now</span>
            <span class="row-title">10k reputation on Stack Overflow en español</span>
          </div>
          <p class="row-desc">
            Mostly C and C++ answers, with a few gold badges along the way.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="record-langs">
        <span class="rl-label">Languages</span>
        <span>Spanish (native), English (B2).</span>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Built with Astro. No JavaScript. Last built {buildDate}.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/mateocerri">GitHub</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mateocerri">LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Base>
